       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine 30 mg once daily is three times the usual maximum adult dose of 10 mg daily. An overdose can cause severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and peripheral edema. In large overdoses it can also cause prolonged shock and non-cardiogenic pulmonary edema.\n\nCan you check the intended dose? Typical adult dosing is:\n- **Starting dose:** 2.5\u20135 mg by mouth once daily.\n- **Usual maintenance dose:** 5\u201310 mg once daily.\n- **Maximum dose:** 10 mg once daily.\n\nThe 30 mg may be a typo, for example for 3 mg or 10 mg. It may also be a mix-up with another drug.\n\nIf you confirm a dose within the usual range, I'll enter it right away. If you really do intend 30 mg, please talk to your supervising resident or attending first. I can then enter it with a note documenting that the dose was verified."
